    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d564">

                <pb facs="0653" n="551" sameAs="frus:frus1927v03/pg551"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">891.51A/372: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Persia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Philip</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Teheran</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1927-06-25T11:00:00+03:25"><hi rendition="#italic">June 25,
                                1927—11 a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received June 25—7:16
                    a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>[43.] Draft of new contract has been submitted formally by Minister of Finance to
                    Millspaugh for his approval. Millspaugh <pb facs="0654" n="552" xml:id="pg552"/>
                    regards new terms as entirely inadmissible, and he is drawing up for the Prime
                    Minister a long exposition of his own views.</p>
                <p>The Minister of Finance, as perhaps also the Government, appears to wish to
                    deprive Doctor Millspaugh and the other Americans of their essential powers and
                    to break up their close unity of organization, or to obtain the resignation of
                    Doctor Millspaugh himself.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Philip</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
